· Meso‑zone: at each room entry, a smaller glyph panel with tactile Tifinagh indicates the room function.
· Micro‑zone: inside rooms, tiny engraved glyphs on fixtures provide equipment labels.

Directional glyphs (stylised Tifinagh arrow ⴰ) are placed at decision points. The wayfinding system meets NASA‑STD‑3001 human‑factors guidelines for legibility (minimum character height 25 mm at 1 m viewing distance) and colour contrast (luminance ratio > 3:1).

