Appendix H – Integration with Life‑Support Systems: Biowall Specifications, Mass and Power Budgets

H.1 Biowall Detailed Design

The courtyard biowall consists of modular panels (1.0 m × 2.0 m) made of food‑grade HDPE with a geotextile felt facing. Nutrient solution is delivered via micro‑drip emitters (2 L/h) from the greywater processing unit. Drainage is collected at the base and returned to the water recycling system. LED grow lights (red 660 nm + blue 450 nm) supplement the fibre‑optic daylighting during lunar night, operating on a 16 h photoperiod.

Daily resource flows (15 m² total):

· Water transpired: 2.5 L (recovered)
· CO₂ fixed: 0.30 kg
· O₂ produced: 0.22 kg
· Biomass harvested (mint, coriander): 0.05 kg fresh weight (edible supplement)

The biowall is managed by the ECLSS controller, which adjusts irrigation and lighting based on humidity, CO₂, and plant health sensors.

H.2 System Mass and Power Budget (Single CDG Module)

