· Build the Moroccan Sahara Analogue Habitat (Erg Chebbi), consisting of one CDG module and one control module.
· Conduct Phase I and Phase II human testing as per Appendix G.
· Publish validation data; refine CRI weights and CDG optimisation parameters.

Phase 3 (2031–2034): Lunar Surface Precursor Mission

· Integrate a single CDG‑designed module (cylindrical core + muqarnas diagrid, simplified courtyard with fountain mock‑up) onto a Commercial Lunar Payload Services (CLPS) lander.
· Robotic teleoperation prints the module over 3–4 lunar days; internal environment is monitored for 1 year (thermal, radiation, structural health).
· No crew; test of automated construction and system robustness.

Phase 4 (2034–): Integration into Permanent Outpost (Artemis Base Camp)

· Full CDG habitat cluster constructed: two riad modules, an agadir storage complex, and a kasbah outer shield wall.
· Crew arrives; initial 180‑day mission with continuous CRI monitoring.
· Re‑semanticisation protocol activated after mission return; ALDC updates motif library based on crew feedback.

Phase 5 (Ongoing): Cross‑Cultural Expansion

· Navajo, Japanese, and other cultural data packages developed and validated.
· CDG becomes a standardised component of international lunar habitat design guidelines, with cultural continuity recognised as a performance requirement alongside radiation protection and structural integrity.

